- op: discuss  # 24d5
  at: '2026-03-05T21:15:26Z'  # 24d5
  by: human  # 24d5
  actor: jgstern  # 24d5
  clock: 5  # 24d5
  nonce: 24d5  # 24d5
  message: "on second thought after remembering what the real issue here was: this should be a noisy and hard gate. the thing we must prevent is the agent modifying production code in the middle of a bakeoff. at the same time, if autonomous mode is active, it should *stay* active. the two are in tension to an extent, but the agent simply needs to either go to sleep or run some analyses that simply do not write to any executable production code files. this must be an editable python package so this is no joke."  # 24d5
- op: update  # c8a2
  at: '2026-03-05T21:19:02Z'  # c8a2
  by: human  # c8a2
  actor: jgstern  # c8a2
  clock: 6  # c8a2
  nonce: c8a2  # c8a2
  set:  # c8a2
    title: "prehook: bakeoff-aware gating (don't modify production code mid-bakeoff)"  # c8a2
    description: "hook should detect running bakeoff processes and block any change to executable production code. Currently judgment-based, not mechanistically enforced. we might not be able to physically prevent the agent from modifying a given file, but we can use a git hook to refuse to commit a file that was modified in the midst of a bakeoff, and then yell at the agent and I guess make it revert the changes"  # c8a2
