  clock: 8  # 86de
  nonce: 86de  # 86de
  set:  # 86de
    description: "hook should detect running bakeoff processes and block any change to executable production code. Currently judgment-based, not mechanistically enforced. we might not be able to physically prevent the agent from modifying a given file, but we can use a git hook to refuse to commit a file that was modified in the midst of a bakeoff, and then yell at the agent and I guess make it revert the changes. NOTE that this doesn't mean no commits are allowed during a bakeoff. the docs can be changed; the tracker can be manipulated and synced as usual. but no changes to the code that is currently executing (or is eligible to execute as a result of running hypergumbo)"  # 86de
